#
#  Reproduces the panel from "Cytokine_Profile Ver3 (non-detects = 0).xlsx".
#  Base R graphics only: no packages to install, runs as-is in RStudio.
#
#  The y-axis is a symmetric-log ("symlog") scale — logarithmic above the kit
#  minimum detection dose, linear below it — because a value of 0 has no
#  position on an ordinary log axis. The transform below is the same one
#  matplotlib's set_yscale("symlog") uses, so the panel is identical.
#
#  Run: source this file (Ctrl+Shift+S / Cmd+Shift+S). The panel is drawn into
#  the RStudio Plots pane; export it yourself with
#      Plots -> Export -> Save as PDF...
#  and set Width 5.6 in, Height 7 in in that dialog so the proportions match
#  what you see here. "Cairo PDF" gives the cleanest text; either works.
#
#  If you get "Error in plot.new(): figure margins too large", the Plots pane is
#  simply too small for the margins - drag it larger, or click Zoom, and re-run.
